{"openapi":"3.1.0","info":{"title":"PennyCompute buyer API","version":"1.10.0","description":"Media jobs over HTTP: video generation with MiniMax H3, FFmpeg work (transcode, stitch, sound mix, captions, timeline exports, frame images and sound files), media measurement and Remotion renders. Create a server API key in the dashboard at https://app.pennycompute.com and send it on every call as Authorization: Bearer <key>. Submit a job to POST /v1/jobs with a service_id and its input, read GET /v1/jobs/{id} until its status is final or register a webhook endpoint, then fetch the file from the link GET /v1/jobs/{id}/output returns. Media goes in by public link; POST /v1/assets hosts one source file or a complete Remotion bundle. h3.video.v1 is text to video with optional first and last frames or reference files; h3.reference_480p.v1 is the earlier one-image preset, kept for existing integrations. Bodies are JSON, up to 2 MB. Amounts are strings in millionths of one US dollar. Each API key may send 600 requests a minute. A request over the limit receives HTTP 429 with the error rate_limited and a Retry-After header in seconds. Job submissions, estimates and capacity reads are each limited to 120 a minute for a key and answer 429 past that. Guides are at https://pennycompute.com/docs, the reference at https://pennycompute.com/docs/api and the dated list of changes at https://pennycompute.com/docs/changes."},"tags":[{"name":"Jobs","description":"Submit work, follow it and fetch the finished file. https://pennycompute.com/docs/jobs says what every answer means."},{"name":"Services","description":"What is sold now and how busy each service is."},{"name":"Uploads","description":"Host a source file or a complete Remotion bundle for a job. Any public link works in a job input without an upload."},{"name":"Webhooks","description":"Be told when a job reaches a final state."},{"name":"Billing","description":"The prepaid balance, charges and statements."},{"name":"Account","description":"Who a key or a signed-in person belongs to."},{"name":"Status","description":"Whether the API is up."},{"name":"Dashboard","description":"Calls the dashboard at https://app.pennycompute.com makes for a signed-in person: keys, top-ups and the people in the organization. A server API key cannot make them."},{"name":"Images","description":"Container images registered for instances. Not offered at present: a start answers 409 no_capacity."},{"name":"Instances","description":"Your own container image, started by name, reached over HTTP and billed by the running second. Not offered at present: a start answers 409 no_capacity."}],"servers":[{"url":"https://api.pennycompute.com"}],"security":[{"buyerKey":[]}],"components":{"securitySchemes":{"buyerKey":{"type":"http","scheme":"bearer","description":"A server API key, created in the dashboard at https://app.pennycompute.com under Server API keys. It starts with pc_live_ and is shown once, when it is created. Send it as Authorization: Bearer <key>. A key carries the scopes jobs:read and jobs:write. Submitting and cancelling jobs, preparing uploads and changing webhook endpoints need jobs:write; listing and reading jobs, usage, invoices and webhook endpoints need jobs:read. A call with no key, or with an unknown or revoked one, answers 401 unauthorized. A key without the scope answers 403 missing_scope."}},"schemas":{"Job":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string","format":"uuid"},"service_id":{"type":"string"},"status":{"type":"string","enum":["queued","active","cancelling","succeeded","failed","cancelled","expired"],"description":"queued: accepted and waiting for a renderer; it occupies no slot. active: a renderer is working on it. cancelling: cancellation was requested while it was running. succeeded: final; the output is ready and the job is charged. failed: final; not charged. cancelled: final; not charged. expired: final; no renderer took it within max_wait_seconds (failure_code no_capacity); not charged."},"failure_code":{"type":["string","null"],"description":"Why a job did not succeed; null otherwise. On failed: download_failed (a link could not be fetched), invalid_input (the media does not fit the input, for example a required sound stream is missing), runner_failed (the render program failed), upload_failed (the finished file could not be stored), lease_expired (the renderer stopped answering), provider_offline (the renderer went away), internal_error (a fault on our side), commit_conflict (the job was finished twice; rare). On expired: no_capacity (no renderer took the job within max_wait_seconds; it never started). On cancelled: buyer_cancelled."},"failure_message":{"type":["string","null"],"description":"A sentence beside failure_code saying what went wrong, for example which link could not be fetched."},"outstanding_micros":{"type":"string","pattern":"^[0-9]+$","description":"Millionths of one US dollar"},"charged_fee_micros":{"type":["string","null"],"description":"Final charge in millionths of a US dollar after successful completion."},"priority":{"type":"string"},"client_reference":{"type":["string","null"]},"output_file":{"type":["object","null"],"description":"What the finished file is. null until the output exists. The output link serves the file under this content type.","properties":{"extension":{"type":"string","enum":["mp4","webm","mov","png","jpg","webp","json","wav","mp3","m4a"]},"content_type":{"type":"string","description":"For example video/mp4 or video/webm."}}},"result":{"type":["object","null"],"additionalProperties":true,"description":"Facts about the output, up to 64 KB, or null until the job completes: duration_seconds, width and height as measured (an image has width and height and no length), plus what the service reports. ffmpeg.timeline_export.v1 adds sound. ffmpeg.frames.v1 adds cells. ffmpeg.audio.v1 reports duration_seconds, sample_rate, channels, integrated_lufs and true_peak_dbtp. media.measure.v1 reports MeasureResult.","properties":{"duration_seconds":{"type":"number"},"width":{"type":"integer"},"height":{"type":"integer"},"sound":{"type":"object","description":"The sound report of a timeline export, measured on the finished file.","properties":{"codec":{"type":"string"},"sample_rate":{"type":"integer"},"channels":{"type":"integer"},"bitrate_kbps":{"type":"number","description":"The measured bitrate of the stream, not the one asked for. A silent or nearly silent mix measures very low, a few kbps, whatever bitrate was asked for."},"duration_seconds":{"type":"number"},"true_peak_dbtp":{"type":["number","null"]},"integrated_lufs":{"type":["number","null"]},"peak_correction_db":{"type":"number","description":"How much lower the final encode is than the first."},"correction_passes":{"type":"integer","description":"How many times the sound was encoded again."}}},"resolved_props":{"description":"For remotion.render.v1 with resolved_props: the resolved props of the named composition, or the value at prop inside them. Any JSON."},"cells":{"type":"array","description":"For ffmpeg.frames.v1: one entry per cell, with the seconds of the frame grabbed from a video, or null for an image.","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"seconds":{"type":["number","null"]}}}}}},"created_at":{"type":"string","format":"date-time","description":"When the job was submitted."},"started_at":{"type":["string","null"],"format":"date-time","description":"When a renderer first took the job, or null while none has. A job that expired with no_capacity, or was cancelled while queued, keeps null. A job tried again on another renderer keeps the first time."},"completed_at":{"type":["string","null"],"format":"date-time","description":"When the job reached succeeded, failed, cancelled or expired, or null until then. Date a charge by this."},"updated_at":{"type":"string","format":"date-time","description":"When the job last changed. On a finished job this is the moment it ended, the same as completed_at: nothing changes it afterwards."}},"required":["id","service_id","status"]},"WebhookEndpoint":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string","format":"uuid"},"name":{"type":"string"},"url":{"type":"string","format":"uri"},"events":{"type":"array","items":{"enum":["job.succeeded","job.failed","job.cancelled"]}},"status":{"enum":["active","disabled"]},"created_at":{"type":"string"},"updated_at":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","name","url","events","status"]},"WebhookEvent":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string","format":"uuid","description":"The delivery ID. The same on every attempt, and in the X-PennyCompute-Delivery header."},"type":{"enum":["job.succeeded","job.failed","job.cancelled"]},"data":{"type":"object","properties":{"job_id":{"type":"string","format":"uuid"},"status":{"enum":["succeeded","failed","expired","cancelled"],"description":"job.failed carries failed or expired."},"failure_code":{"type":"string","description":"On job.failed and job.cancelled. The codes are those of the job read."},"message":{"type":"string","description":"A sentence beside failure_code."}},"required":["job_id","status"]}},"required":["id","type","data"],"examples":[{"id":"5b0e6f0a-2c3d-4e5f-8a9b-0c1d2e3f4a5b","type":"job.succeeded","data":{"job_id":"7d484be8-7f2f-411f-840e-9ff06b6f725a","status":"succeeded"}},{"id":"0a1b2c3d-4e5f-4a6b-8c7d-9e0f1a2b3c4d","type":"job.failed","data":{"job_id":"7d484be8-7f2f-411f-840e-9ff06b6f725a","status":"failed","failure_code":"download_failed","message":"a link could not be fetched"}}]},"Specification":{"type":"object","properties":{"service_id":{"type":"string","enum":["h3.video.v1","h3.reference_480p.v1","ffmpeg.transcode.v1","ffmpeg.stitch_export.v1","ffmpeg.audio_mix.v1","ffmpeg.caption_burn.v1","ffmpeg.timeline_export.v1","ffmpeg.frames.v1","ffmpeg.audio.v1","media.measure.v1","remotion.render.v1"],"description":"A service listed by GET /v1/services."},"input":{"description":"The schema depends on service_id. The FFmpeg services take the inputs in FfmpegTranscodeInput, FfmpegStitchInput, FfmpegCaptionBurnInput, FfmpegAudioMixInput, FfmpegTimelineExportInput, FfmpegFramesInput and FfmpegAudioInput. media.measure.v1 takes MediaMeasureInput. remotion.render.v1 takes RemotionRenderInput.","anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/H3VideoInput"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/H3PresetInput"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/FfmpegTranscodeInput"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/FfmpegStitchInput"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/FfmpegCaptionBurnInput"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/FfmpegAudioMixInput"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/FfmpegTimelineExportInput"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/FfmpegFramesInput"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/FfmpegAudioInput"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/MediaMeasureInput"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/RemotionRenderInput"}]},"max_wait_seconds":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":86400,"default":900,"description":"How long a queued job waits for a renderer. After that it becomes expired with failure_code no_capacity and is not charged."},"client_reference":{"type":"string","maxLength":256,"description":"Your own reference, returned on the job."},"priority":{"enum":["normal","batch"],"default":"normal","description":"batch yields to normal jobs in the queue. Every buyer shares one queue; no faster class is sold."},"webhook_endpoint_id":{"type":"string","format":"uuid","description":"Send this job’s events to one registered endpoint only. Without it, events go to every active endpoint of the organization."}},"required":["service_id","input"],"allOf":[{"if":{"properties":{"service_id":{"const":"h3.video.v1"}},"required":["service_id"]},"then":{"properties":{"input":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/H3VideoInput"}}}},{"if":{"properties":{"service_id":{"const":"h3.reference_480p.v1"}},"required":["service_id"]},"then":{"properties":{"input":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/H3PresetInput"}}}}]},"EstimateRequest":{"type":"object","properties":{"service_id":{"type":"string","enum":["h3.video.v1","h3.reference_480p.v1","ffmpeg.transcode.v1","ffmpeg.stitch_export.v1","ffmpeg.audio_mix.v1","ffmpeg.caption_burn.v1","ffmpeg.timeline_export.v1","ffmpeg.frames.v1","ffmpeg.audio.v1","media.measure.v1","remotion.render.v1"],"description":"A service listed by GET /v1/services."},"input":{"description":"The schema depends on service_id. The FFmpeg services take the inputs in FfmpegTranscodeInput, FfmpegStitchInput, FfmpegCaptionBurnInput, FfmpegAudioMixInput, FfmpegTimelineExportInput, FfmpegFramesInput and FfmpegAudioInput. media.measure.v1 takes MediaMeasureInput. remotion.render.v1 takes RemotionRenderInput.","anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/H3VideoInput"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/H3PresetInput"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/FfmpegTranscodeInput"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/FfmpegStitchInput"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/FfmpegCaptionBurnInput"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/FfmpegAudioMixInput"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/FfmpegTimelineExportInput"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/FfmpegFramesInput"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/FfmpegAudioInput"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/MediaMeasureInput"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/RemotionRenderInput"}]},"max_wait_seconds":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":86400,"default":900,"description":"How long a queued job waits for a renderer. After that it becomes expired with failure_code no_capacity and is not charged."}},"required":["service_id","input"]},"Estimate":{"type":"object","properties":{"service_id":{"type":"string"},"price_micros":{"type":"string","pattern":"^[0-9]+$","description":"Price in millionths of one US dollar. Remotion price_micros does not come from opening the bundle or reading the composition. It is based on frame_range when provided (the inclusive frame count divided by 30 fps), or a 20-second default when frame_range is absent. It is not the final charge: price_is_final is false, and the completed job is charged for its actual output."},"price_is_final":{"type":"boolean","description":"true for H3: the price is final for the given options. false for FFmpeg, measurement and Remotion work, which is billed on completion for what the job made: the length of a video or a sound file, or one flat price for an image or a measurement."},"estimated_render_seconds":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"description":"Typical render time once a renderer starts the job. Queue time is extra."},"free_slots":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"description":"Jobs like this one that could start now."},"running_jobs":{"type":"integer","minimum":0},"queued_jobs":{"type":"integer","minimum":0},"estimated_start_seconds":{"type":"array","minItems":2,"maxItems":2,"items":{"type":"integer","minimum":0},"description":"Low and high estimate of the seconds from now until the job starts."},"estimated_complete_seconds":{"type":"array","minItems":2,"maxItems":2,"items":{"type":"integer","minimum":0},"description":"Low and high estimate of the seconds from now until the job completes."},"max_wait_seconds":{"type":"integer","description":"The queue wait limit this estimate assumed."}},"required":["service_id","price_micros","price_is_final","estimated_render_seconds","free_slots","running_jobs","queued_jobs","estimated_start_seconds","estimated_complete_seconds","max_wait_seconds"]},"Capacity":{"type":"object","properties":{"service_id":{"type":"string"},"free_slots":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"description":"Jobs of this service that could start now. For H3 it counts a fast-quality clip."},"running_jobs":{"type":"integer","minimum":0},"queued_jobs":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}},"required":["service_id","free_slots","running_jobs","queued_jobs"]},"Error":{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string","description":"A stable code to branch on. On any call: unauthorized (401, no key, or one that is unknown or revoked), missing_scope (403, the key lacks jobs:read or jobs:write), not_found (404, no such path, or nothing with that ID in your organization), rate_limited (429). internal_error (500) and supplier_unavailable (502) are faults on our side: send the request again. Each operation lists the codes of its own."},"issues":{"type":"array","description":"Present when error is invalid_request: the input fields that were refused.","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"field":{"type":"string"},"message":{"type":"string"}},"required":["field","message"]}}},"required":["error"]},"H3VideoInput":{"type":"object","properties":{"prompt":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":10000,"description":"What happens in the shot, how the camera moves and what we hear. Line breaks are allowed. A plain sentence is laid out for the model automatically and gets ambient sound. To direct sound, write the model’s own fields and the prompt is sent as written: spoken lines as <d>…</d>, an overall_soundscape: line and a non_diegetic_music: line. A prompt on a request with references is always sent as written."},"public_intent":{"type":"boolean","description":"No longer needed. Accepted and ignored."},"duration_seconds":{"type":"integer","minimum":4,"maximum":10,"default":5,"description":"Clip length in seconds. Output is 24 fps and the model generates in 17-frame chunks, so the delivered length is within about a third of a second of the request: 5 seconds is 124 frames, 10 is 243, 15 is 362. A 4-second request returns 107 frames. The longest clip is 10 seconds at 480p and 5 seconds at 768p."},"resolution":{"enum":["480p","768p"],"default":"480p","description":"768p is the model’s native size. 2K is not offered."},"aspect_ratio":{"enum":["16:9","9:16","1:1","4:3","3:4","21:9"],"default":"16:9","description":"Output size in pixels. 480p: 16:9 is 864×480, 9:16 is 480×864, 1:1 is 640×640, 4:3 is 736×544, 3:4 is 544×736, 21:9 is 992×416. 768p: 16:9 is 1344×768, 9:16 is 768×1344, 1:1 is 1024×1024, 4:3 is 1152×864, 3:4 is 864×1152, 21:9 is 1568×672."},"quality":{"enum":["fast","high","full"],"default":"fast","description":"fast runs 4 to 5 passes with a distilled adapter; high runs 20 passes and reuses work in the middle steps; full runs 20 full passes. More passes take longer to render and cost more."},"seed":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"maximum":2147483647,"description":"Omit it and every job gets a fresh random seed, so repeating a prompt gives a different clip. Pass it and the same request reproduces the same clip."},"first_frame_url":{"type":"string","format":"uri","pattern":"^https?://","maxLength":4096,"description":"The clip starts on this JPEG or PNG image. It is scaled and centre-cropped to the output size. Any public link to the file, or an input_url from POST /v1/assets. The renderer downloads it when the job starts, so the link has to stay readable until then."},"last_frame_url":{"type":"string","format":"uri","pattern":"^https?://","maxLength":4096,"description":"The clip ends on this JPEG or PNG image. It is scaled and centre-cropped to the output size. Any public link to the file, or an input_url from POST /v1/assets. The renderer downloads it when the job starts, so the link has to stay readable until then."},"references":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/H3References"}},"required":["prompt"],"additionalProperties":false,"not":{"anyOf":[{"required":["references","first_frame_url"]},{"required":["references","last_frame_url"]}]},"description":"Input for h3.video.v1: text to video with optional frames or references. Unknown fields are rejected. Send no media for text to video; first_frame_url, last_frame_url or both to start or end on an image; or references. Output is an MP4 with H.264 video at 24 fps and stereo AAC audio. The price depends on length, resolution, quality and references: POST /v1/jobs/estimate returns it. A five-second 480p clip at fast quality from text, frames or one reference image costs 25000 micros ($0.025). Options that would render for more than 30 minutes are refused with invalid_request.","examples":[{"prompt":"A lighthouse on a rocky headland at sunset. The camera pulls back slowly over the water. Soft wind and distant surf."},{"prompt":"The camera pulls back slowly from the lighthouse.","duration_seconds":8,"resolution":"480p","aspect_ratio":"16:9","quality":"fast","seed":7,"first_frame_url":"https://example.com/lighthouse.jpg"},{"prompt":"<Picture 1> Slowly pull back from the lighthouse. Soft wind and distant surf.","references":{"images":["https://example.com/lighthouse.jpg"]}}]},"H3References":{"type":"object","properties":{"images":{"type":"array","maxItems":9,"items":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/MediaUrl"},"description":"JPEG or PNG images. Name them in the prompt in order as <Picture 1>, <Picture 2>."},"videos":{"type":"array","maxItems":3,"items":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/H3ReferenceClip"},"description":"MP4 videos, at most 15 seconds in total. Name them in the prompt in order as <Video 1>, <Video 2>."},"audio":{"type":"array","maxItems":3,"items":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/H3ReferenceClip"},"description":"WAV or M4A audio, at most 15 seconds in total. Name the clips in the prompt in order as <Audio 1>, <Audio 2>. Audio needs an image or video beside it."},"use_video_sound":{"type":"boolean","default":false,"description":"Include the sound of the reference videos. Needs at least one reference video."}},"required":[],"additionalProperties":false,"description":"Reference files for the model to draw on. At least one file and at most 12 in all. Cannot be combined with first_frame_url or last_frame_url."},"H3ReferenceClip":{"type":"object","properties":{"url":{"type":"string","format":"uri","pattern":"^https?://","maxLength":4096,"description":"Any public link to the file, or an input_url from POST /v1/assets. The renderer downloads it when the job starts, so the link has to stay readable until then."},"seconds":{"type":"integer","minimum":2,"maximum":15,"description":"How much of the clip is used, from its start."}},"required":["url"],"additionalProperties":false},"MediaUrl":{"type":"string","format":"uri","pattern":"^https?://","maxLength":4096,"description":"Any public link to the file, or an input_url from POST /v1/assets. The renderer downloads it when the job starts, so the link has to stay readable until then."},"H3PresetInput":{"type":"object","properties":{"prompt":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":2000,"description":"One line, sent to the model as written. Refer to the image as <Picture 1>."},"reference_jpeg_base64":{"type":"string","maxLength":180000,"description":"One JPEG, base64-encoded, at most 180,000 characters."},"public_intent":{"type":"boolean","description":"No longer needed. Accepted and ignored."},"seed":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"maximum":2147483647,"description":"Omit it and every job gets a fresh random seed, so repeating a prompt gives a different clip. Pass it and the same request reproduces the same clip."}},"required":["prompt","reference_jpeg_base64"],"additionalProperties":false,"description":"Input for h3.reference_480p.v1, the original published preset, kept unchanged for existing integrations: one inline JPEG and a prompt in, a fixed five-second 864×480 MP4 with stereo AAC audio out, for 25000 micros ($0.025). seed is its only addition. Use h3.video.v1 for new work."},"FfmpegTranscodeInput":{"type":"object","properties":{"input_url":{"type":"string","format":"uri","description":"Any public https link to the file, up to 1 GB, or an input_url from POST /v1/assets. The renderer fetches it with a plain GET, so keep it readable until the job has ended."},"video_codec":{"type":"string","enum":["h264_videotoolbox","libx264"],"description":"h264_videotoolbox encodes on the renderer hardware. libx264 encodes in software.","default":"h264_videotoolbox"},"audio_codec":{"type":"string","enum":["aac","copy"],"default":"aac"},"height":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":2160,"description":"Output height in pixels. Omit to keep the source height."},"start_seconds":{"type":"number","minimum":0,"maximum":86400,"description":"Keep one part of the source, from here. May be given without duration_seconds."},"duration_seconds":{"type":"number","minimum":0.01,"maximum":86400,"description":"How much of the source to keep."},"fps":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":120,"description":"The output frame rate."},"keep_fps_at_least":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":120,"description":"With fps: a source whose own rate is at least this keeps its rate. Refused without fps."},"strip_audio":{"type":"boolean","description":"The output has no sound stream."},"pad_to_duration_seconds":{"type":"number","minimum":0.01,"maximum":86400,"description":"When the result is shorter, its last frame is kept on screen, with silence, up to this length. A result that is already as long is left as it is."},"overlay_image_url":{"type":"string","format":"uri","description":"One image laid over the whole picture for its whole length, stretched to the frame as it is after height. Its transparency is kept."},"replace_audio_url":{"type":"string","format":"uri","description":"A sound file that replaces the soundtrack. It is cut at the length of the picture or padded with silence up to it. Refused together with strip_audio."},"replace_audio_in_seconds":{"type":"number","minimum":0,"maximum":86400,"default":0,"description":"Where in replace_audio_url the new sound starts."}},"required":["input_url"],"description":"Input for ffmpeg.transcode.v1. audio_codec copy works with a cut, a frame rate and an overlay; it is refused with replace_audio_url, and with pad_to_duration_seconds unless strip_audio is set, because both write new sound."},"FfmpegStitchInput":{"type":"object","properties":{"input_urls":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","format":"uri","description":"Any public https link to the file, up to 1 GB, or an input_url from POST /v1/assets. The renderer fetches it with a plain GET, so keep it readable until the job has ended."},"minItems":1,"maxItems":64,"description":"Clips in playback order, joined end to end."},"video_codec":{"type":"string","enum":["copy","h264_videotoolbox","libx264"],"default":"copy","description":"copy joins the clips without re-encoding; they must share codec, size, frame rate and audio layout. The other values re-encode."},"audio_codec":{"type":"string","enum":["copy","aac"],"default":"copy"},"output_container":{"type":"string","enum":["mp4"],"default":"mp4"}},"required":["input_urls"]},"FfmpegCaptionBurnInput":{"type":"object","properties":{"input_url":{"type":"string","format":"uri","description":"Any public https link to the file, up to 1 GB, or an input_url from POST /v1/assets. The renderer fetches it with a plain GET, so keep it readable until the job has ended."},"captions_url":{"type":"string","format":"uri","description":"Any public https link to the file, up to 1 GB, or an input_url from POST /v1/assets. The renderer fetches it with a plain GET, so keep it readable until the job has ended."},"captions_format":{"type":"string","enum":["ass","srt"],"default":"ass"}},"required":["input_url","captions_url"]},"FfmpegAudioMixInput":{"type":"object","properties":{"input_url":{"type":"string","format":"uri","description":"Any public https link to the file, up to 1 GB, or an input_url from POST /v1/assets. The renderer fetches it with a plain GET, so keep it readable until the job has ended."},"tracks":{"type":"array","minItems":1,"maxItems":16,"items":{"type":"object","properties":{"input_url":{"type":"string","format":"uri","description":"Any public https link to the file, up to 1 GB, or an input_url from POST /v1/assets. The renderer fetches it with a plain GET, so keep it readable until the job has ended."},"role":{"type":"string","enum":["dialogue","music","effect"]},"start_ms":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"maximum":86400000,"default":0},"gain_db":{"type":"number","minimum":-60,"maximum":12,"default":0},"loop":{"type":"boolean","default":false}},"required":["input_url","role"]}},"preserve_source_audio":{"type":"boolean","default":true},"ducking":{"type":"object","properties":{"enabled":{"type":"boolean","default":true},"threshold_db":{"type":"number","minimum":-60,"maximum":0,"default":-24},"ratio":{"type":"number","minimum":1,"maximum":20,"default":8},"attack_ms":{"type":"number","minimum":1,"maximum":2000,"default":20},"release_ms":{"type":"number","minimum":10,"maximum":5000,"default":250}},"required":[]},"output_audio_bitrate_kbps":{"type":"integer","minimum":64,"maximum":512,"default":192}},"required":["input_url","tracks"]},"FfmpegTimelineExportInput":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"picture":{"type":"string","enum":["encode","copy"],"default":"encode","description":"encode: the picture is made from clips or picture_segments on the canvas. copy: the picture of source_url is kept untouched and only its sound is replaced or finished."},"canvas":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"aspect_ratio":{"type":"string","enum":["16:9","9:16","1:1","4:3"]},"resolution":{"type":"string","enum":["720p","1080p","4k","proxy_480p"],"default":"720p"},"fps":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":120,"default":30},"crf":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"maximum":51,"description":"The quality of every picture encode in the job: lower is a better picture and a larger file. Left out, it follows resolution: 30 at proxy_480p, 23 at 720p, 18 at 1080p and 20 at 4k. It does not change the price."},"preset":{"type":"string","enum":["ultrafast","superfast","veryfast","faster","fast","medium","slow","slower","veryslow"],"description":"The libx264 preset of every picture encode in the job. Left out, it follows resolution: fast at proxy_480p and 720p, veryfast at 1080p and 4k. It does not change the price."}},"required":["aspect_ratio"],"description":"The output shape, size and frame rate. Required for an encoded picture; a copied picture keeps its own size."},"duration_seconds":{"type":"number","minimum":0.1,"maximum":3600,"description":"The total length of the output. Picture is padded with black and 