"items":{"type":"string","enum":["format","loudness","scenes","black","freeze"]},"description":"What to measure. format: container, length, size, and the video and sound streams. loudness: integrated loudness, true peak and loudness range. scenes: the times of cuts. black: stretches of black from 0.1 seconds. freeze: stretches of frozen picture from 0.5 seconds."},"scene_threshold":{"type":"number","minimum":0.01,"maximum":1,"default":0.3,"description":"How different two frames must be to count as a cut."},"waveform":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"width":{"type":"integer","minimum":16,"maximum":4096},"height":{"type":"integer","minimum":16,"maximum":1024}},"required":["width","height"],"description":"A picture of the sound waveform at this size in pixels. It becomes the output file."}},"required":["url","measures"],"description":"Input for media.measure.v1: facts about one media file. Unknown fields are refused. The measurements come back as the job result, one entry per measure asked for; a list is cut at 500 entries and then carries truncated: true. The output file is the waveform PNG when one is asked for, otherwise the same measurements as a JSON file.","examples":[{"url":"https://example.com/take.mp4","measures":["format","loudness","scenes"]},{"url":"https://example.com/song.mp3","measures":["loudness"],"waveform":{"width":1200,"height":200}}]},"MeasureResult":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"format":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"duration_seconds":{"type":["number","null"]},"size_bytes":{"type":"integer"},"container":{"type":"string"},"video":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"codec":{"type":"string"},"width":{"type":"integer"},"height":{"type":"integer"},"fps":{"type":["number","null"]},"rotation_degrees":{"type":"number","description":"How far the stored frame is turned clockwise for display."},"pixel_format":{"type":["string","null"]},"color_space":{"type":["string","null"]}},"required":[]},"audio":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"codec":{"type":"string"},"sample_rate":{"type":"integer"},"channels":{"type":"integer"}},"required":[]}},"required":[]},"loudness":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"integrated_lufs":{"type":["number","null"]},"true_peak_dbtp":{"type":["number","null"]},"loudness_range_lu":{"type":["number","null"]}},"required":[]},"scenes":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"cuts_seconds":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"number"}},"truncated":{"const":true}},"required":[]},"black":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"ranges":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"start_seconds":{"type":"number"},"end_seconds":{"type":"number"}},"required":[]}},"truncated":{"const":true}},"required":[]},"freeze":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"ranges":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"start_seconds":{"type":"number"},"end_seconds":{"type":"number"}},"required":[]}},"truncated":{"const":true}},"required":[]}},"required":[],"description":"The result of a media.measure.v1 job: one entry for each measure asked for."},"RemotionRenderInput":{"type":"object","properties":{"serve_url":{"type":"string","format":"uri","description":"Public link to your bundled Remotion site: the index.html written by npx remotion bundle. To host it here, send the bundle’s file manifest to POST /v1/assets, PUT every returned upload, and use its serve_url on the isolated quiet-field-7f3c.buildngrowsv.workers.dev bundle origin."},"composition_id":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200,"description":"The composition to render."},"input_props":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true,"default":{},"description":"Props passed to the composition. Any JSON."},"input_props_url":{"type":"string","format":"uri","pattern":"^https?://","description":"Public link to the props as a JSON object, up to 64 MB. Use it for props too large to send in the request. Not together with a non-empty input_props."},"still_frame":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"maximum":1000000,"description":"Render this one frame as a PNG in place of a video. The output is a .png. frame_range, crf, the bitrate fields, color_space and the sound fields are refused with it."},"remote_assets":{"type":"array","maxItems":64,"default":[],"description":"Media the composition needs. The renderer downloads each file and writes its local path into input_props before rendering.","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"url":{"type":"string","format":"uri","description":"Public https link to the file, up to 1 GB."},"input_props_path":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200,"description":"Dot-path in input_props that receives the downloaded file, for example voiceover.src or scenes.0.backgroundUrl."}},"required":["url","input_props_path"]}},"bundle_manifest_url":{"type":"string","format":"uri","description":"Not needed for a render: the renderer opens serve_url itself. Accepted and not used. If sent, send bundle_manifest_sha256 with it."},"bundle_manifest_sha256":{"type":"string","pattern":"^[a-f0-9]{64}$","description":"Not needed for a render. Accepted and not used."},"frame_range":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"integer","minimum":0},"minItems":2,"maxItems":2,"description":"First and last frame to render, inclusive. Omit to render every frame."},"output_container":{"type":"string","enum":["mp4","webm","mov"],"default":"mp4"},"video_codec":{"type":"string","enum":["h264","h265","vp8","vp9","prores"],"default":"h264","description":"webm needs vp8 or vp9."},"image_format":{"type":"string","enum":["jpeg","png"],"default":"jpeg","description":"How each frame is captured before encoding. jpeg frames are captured at quality 80."},"crf":{"type":"number","minimum":0,"maximum":51,"description":"Omit for 18 with h264."},"x264_preset":{"type":"string","enum":["ultrafast","superfast","veryfast","faster","fast","medium","slow","slower","veryslow","placebo"],"description":"Only with video_codec h264. Omit for medium. Refused with still_frame."},"x264_profile":{"type":"string","enum":["baseline","main","high"],"description":"Only with video_codec h264. Omit for the encoder choice, which is high with the default settings. Refused with still_frame."},"b_frames":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"maximum":16,"description":"Only with video_codec h264. 0 turns B-frames off. Omit for the encoder choice, two with the default settings. Refused with still_frame."},"jpeg_quality":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"maximum":100,"description":"Quality of the captured frames. Only with image_format jpeg. Omit for 80. Refused with still_frame."},"video_bitrate":{"type":"string","maxLength":16,"pattern":"^[0-9]+(\\.[0-9]+)?[KkM]$","description":"Video bitrate, for example 6M or 800K. Not together with crf."},"encoding_max_rate":{"type":"string","maxLength":16,"pattern":"^[0-9]+(\\.[0-9]+)?[KkM]$","description":"Highest bitrate the encoder may reach. Needs encoding_buffer_size."},"encoding_buffer_size":{"type":"string","maxLength":16,"pattern":"^[0-9]+(\\.[0-9]+)?[KkM]$"},"color_space":{"type":"string","enum":["default","bt709","bt2020-ncl"],"description":"Omit for default, which applies no BT.709 conversion or tag. Send bt709 for a BT.709 file."},"muted":{"type":"boolean","description":"Render with no sound. Not together with audio_codec, audio_bitrate or enforce_audio_track."},"audio_codec":{"type":"string","enum":["aac","mp3","opus","pcm-16"],"description":"pcm-16 needs output_container mov. The pairing has to be one Remotion allows with the video codec."},"audio_bitrate":{"type":"string","maxLength":16,"pattern":"^[0-9]+(\\.[0-9]+)?[KkM]$","description":"Sound bitrate, for example 320K."},"sample_rate":{"type":"integer","minimum":8000,"maximum":96000,"description":"Sound sample rate in hertz. Omit for 48000. Refused with muted and with still_frame."},"enforce_audio_track":{"type":"boolean","description":"Write a sound track even when the composition has no sound."},"gl":{"type":"string","enum":["angle","swangle","egl","vulkan","angle-egl","swiftshader"],"description":"How the browser draws WebGL. Omit for the browser default on a renderer with a real GPU. swangle draws in software, for a render that must not depend on the GPU."},"timeout_ms":{"type":"integer","minimum":7000,"maximum":600000,"description":"How long a frame may wait on the page before the render fails."},"ignore_certificate_errors":{"type":"boolean"},"pixel_format":{"type":"string","enum":["yuv420p","yuva420p","yuv422p","yuv444p"],"default":"yuv420p"},"resolved_props":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["composition_id"],"description":"After the render or still succeeds, select this composition in the same bundle, with the job props and browser settings, without rendering it, and return its resolved props, what its calculateMetadata returns, as result.resolved_props. With prop, only the value at that path is returned, and a missing path gives null. A value too large for the 64 KB result fails the job with invalid_input: name a smaller prop.","properties":{"composition_id":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200},"prop":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200,"description":"A dot path of names inside the resolved props."}}},"concurrency":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":32,"description":"Frames rendered at once. Omit for half the logical cores of the renderer that takes the job, between 1 and 8, so it differs between renderers."}},"required":["serve_url","composition_id"],"description":"Input for remotion.render.v1. Build the bundle with Remotion 4.0.530, the version the renderers run; the bundle carries its own React. The renderer opens the bundle from serve_url in its own browser, so keep the bundle readable at that link until the job has ended. The page loads https media named in its props by itself; remote_assets is for media the page cannot fetch. With nothing else set, a render is H.264 in an MP4 at CRF 18 with the x264 preset medium, frames captured as JPEG at quality 80, yuv420p, and AAC sound at 320 kbps and 48,000 Hz; a composition with no sound gets no sound stream unless enforce_audio_track is true. Hardware encoding is off. Bundle every font the composition draws with: system fonts differ between renderers."},"ApiKey":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string","format":"uuid"},"name":{"type":"string"},"key_prefix":{"type":"string"},"scopes":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","enum":["jobs:read","jobs:write"]}},"created_at":{"type":"string"},"last_used_at":{"type":["string","null"]},"revoked_at":{"type":["string","null"]}},"required":["id"]},"Member":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string","format":"uuid"},"email":{"type":"string"},"display_name":{"type":"string"},"role":{"type":"string","enum":["owner","admin","developer","billing"],"description":"owner: everything, including acting on other owners. admin: everything except acting on owners. developer: jobs, uploads, instances, images, webhooks and server API keys. billing: adds funds and reads jobs, usage and statements."},"verified":{"type":"boolean"},"created_at":{"type":"string"},"last_login_at":{"type":["string","null"]}},"required":["id","email","role"]},"Invitation":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string","format":"uuid"},"email":{"type":"string"},"role":{"type":"string","enum":["owner","admin","developer","billing"],"description":"owner: everything, including acting on other owners. admin: everything except acting on owners. developer: jobs, uploads, instances, images, webhooks and server API keys. billing: adds funds and reads jobs, usage and statements."},"created_at":{"type":"string"},"expires_at":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","email","role"]},"Image":{"type":"object","properties":{"digest":{"type":"string","pattern":"^sha256:[0-9a-f]{64}$","description":"The image digest, as printed by the push to your registry."},"name":{"type":"string"},"source":{"type":"string","description":"The registry and repository the image was copied from."},"state":{"type":"string","enum":["copying","distributing","held","failed"],"description":"copying: being fetched from your registry. distributing: stored, the machines are fetching it. held: at least one machine holds it and a start can be placed. failed: the copy stopped; see error."},"error":{"type":"string","enum":["source_unauthorized","source_not_found","source_unavailable","source_rate_limited","digest_mismatch","invalid_manifest","unsupported_layer","no_linux_platform","layer_too_large","image_too_large","image_storage_full"]},"size_bytes":{"type":"integer","description":"Compressed size of every stored layer."},"platforms":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"architecture":{"type":"string","enum":["amd64","arm64"]},"size_bytes":{"type":"integer"}},"required":[]}},"machines_holding":{"type":"integer","description":"Machines that hold the image now."},"created_at":{"type":"string","format":"date-time"}},"required":["digest","name","state","machines_holding"]},"ImageSource":{"type":"object","properties":{"source":{"type":"string","description":"An image reference in any registry that speaks the OCI distribution API, for example ghcr.io/acme/renderer@sha256:… . A tag is read once and held as its digest. Images for linux/amd64 and linux/arm64 are copied. Each layer up to 5 GB, one image up to 20 GiB."},"username":{"type":"string","description":"Username of a read credential, when your registry needs one."},"password":{"type":"string","description":"Password or access token for the read credential."},"name":{"type":"string","pattern":"^[a-z0-9]+(?:[._-][a-z0-9]+)*$","description":"A display name. Defaults to the last part of the repository."}},"required":["source"]},"Instance":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"name":{"type":"string"},"state":{"type":"string","enum":["starting","running","stopped","crashed","lost"],"description":"starting: placed, not yet answering. running: answering. stopped: ended on purpose; see end_reason. crashed: the container exited. lost: its machine went away."},"end_reason":{"type":"string","enum":["idle","destroyed","lifetime","exited","disk"],"description":"Why it ended. stopped: idle, destroyed or lifetime. crashed: exited (the process ended) or disk (it outgrew disk_gb)."},"exit_code":{"type":"integer","description":"The exit code of a crashed container, when known."},"address":{"type":"string","format":"uri","description":"Send HTTP here with the header Authorization: Bearer <token>. Any method and path; bodies are streamed both ways; one request may stay open 15 minutes. WebSocket upgrades are not carried. Have your container send Content-Length on a reply whose completeness matters, or check the size or framing of what you receive: when an instance ends or its machine goes away in the middle of a reply, a reply without Content-Length ends at the caller as a complete 200 with fewer bytes, and one with Content-Length fails as a broken transfer. Keep connections open in your server (the default in Node, Go and uvicorn): a server that closes its connection after every reply can lose the end of a reply larger than about a megabyte. An answer from PennyCompute rather than from your container carries the header pennycompute-instance with the instance state and a JSON error: 401 invalid_token, 410 instance_gone once the instance has ended, 503 instance_starting when the port has not opened within 30 seconds of the request arriving (a request sent while the instance is starting is held and forwarded when it is ready), 502 instance_unreachable when the container refuses the connection."},"max_request_body_bytes":{"type":"integer","description":"The largest single request body this instance can receive. Replies are not limited."},"token":{"type":"string","description":"Bearer token for the instance address. Returned by a start only."},"image":{"type":"string","pattern":"^sha256:[0-9a-f]{64}$","description":"The image digest, as printed by the push to your registry."},"label":{"type":"string"},"vcpu":{"type":"number","minimum":0.25,"maximum":16,"multipleOf":0.25,"description":"Cores reserved and billed, in quarters. The container sees the next whole number of cores."},"memory_mib":{"type":"integer","minimum":256,"maximum":65536},"disk_gb":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":100,"default":8},"port":{"type":"integer"},"idle_stop_seconds":{"type":"integer"},"max_lifetime_seconds":{"type":"integer"},"rate_nanos_per_second":{"type":"integer","description":"The price of this instance in billionths of a US dollar per running second: 16000 per vCPU, 2000 per GiB of memory, 50 per GB of disk."},"created_at":{"type":"string","format":"date-time"},"started_at":{"type":"string","format":"date-time"},"ended_at":{"type":"string","format":"date-time"},"running_seconds":{"type":"integer","description":"Whole seconds from answering to stopping, so far."},"charge_micros":{"type":"string","pattern":"^[0-9]+$","description":"The charge so far, in millionths of a US dollar."}},"required":["id","name","state","charge_micros"]},"InstanceStart":{"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string","pattern":"^[A-Za-z0-9._:-]{1,128}$","description":"Your name for the instance. A start with the name of an instance that is starting or running returns that instance."},"image":{"type":"string","pattern":"^sha256:[0-9a-f]{64}$","description":"The image digest, as printed by the push to your registry."},"vcpu":{"type":"number","minimum":0.25,"maximum":16,"multipleOf":0.25,"description":"Cores reserved and billed, in quarters. The container sees the next whole number of cores."},"memory_mib":{"type":"integer","minimum":256,"maximum":65536},"disk_gb":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":100,"default":8},"env":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":{"type":"string"},"description":"Environment variables for the container. Up to 64."},"port":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":65535,"default":8080,"description":"The port your container listens on. Requests to the instance address arrive there."},"idle_stop_seconds":{"type":"integer","minimum":5,"maximum":3600,"default":30,"description":"Stop after this long with no request open."},"max_lifetime_seconds":{"type":"integer","minimum":60,"maximum":86400,"default":3600,"description":"Stop this long after the start, whatever is running."},"label":{"type":"string","pattern":"^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._:/-]{0,63}$","description":"Groups instances in usage."},"min_request_body_bytes":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"maximum":4294967296,"default":0,"description":"The largest single request body you will send to this instance. The instance is placed where that body can be carried, or the start is refused with no_capacity. Leave it out for bodies up to 100 MB."}},"required":["name","image","vcpu","memory_mib"]}}},"paths":{"/v1/services":{"get":{"operationId":"listServices","tags":["Services"],"summary":"List enabled services","responses":{"200":{"description":"Success","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"services":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"service_id":{"type":"string"},"display_name":{"type":"string"}},"required":[]}}},"required":[]}}}},"default":{"description":"Request error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Error"}}}}},"security":[]}},"/v1/services/{service_id}/capacity":{"parameters":[{"name":"service_id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","enum":["h3.video.v1","h3.reference_480p.v1","ffmpeg.transcode.v1","ffmpeg.stitch_export.v1","ffmpeg.audio_mix.v1","ffmpeg.caption_burn.v1","ffmpeg.timeline_export.v1","ffmpeg.frames.v1","ffmpeg.audio.v1","media.measure.v1","remotion.render.v1"]}}],"get":{"operationId":"getServiceCapacity","tags":["Services"],"summary":"Read how busy a service is","description":"Counts only: how many jobs could start now, how many are running and how many are queued.","responses":{"200":{"description":"Success","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Capacity"}}}},"404":{"description":"not_found: the service is not offered.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Error"}}}},"default":{"description":"Request error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Error"}}}}}}},"/v1/assets":{"post":{"operationId":"createUpload","tags":["Uploads"],"summary":"Prepare source uploads","description":"Hosts one source file, or a complete Remotion bundle. For one file, returns an upload_url that is also its input_url. For a bundle, send every path, byte length and SHA-256 together; the response gives each upload_url and one serve_url whose relative files are served from the same folder on the isolated quiet-field-7f3c.buildngrowsv.workers.dev origin. That origin has no API, session or cookies; api.pennycompute.com refuses bundle reads. A bundle can have up to 256 nonempty files of up to 100000000 bytes each and 1000000000 bytes in all. Files stop being served 24 hours from their PUT and are swept after a further 48-hour margin. Responses carry X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff. Single-file responses also carry Content-Security-Policy: sandbox; default-src 'none'; bundle HTML carries a separate Content-Security-Policy that permits Remotion’s inline configuration, same-origin scripts and public HTTPS media. Any other public link works in a job input without an upload.","requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"oneOf":[{"type":"object","properties":{"sha256":{"type":"string","pattern":"^[0-9a-f]{64}$","description":"SHA-256 of the file, in hex. The file is then named by it: the same bytes always get the same link, so a job sent again with the same files and the same Idempotency-Key is the same request. An upload whose bytes do not match is refused with digest_mismatch."},"content_type":{"type":"string","minLength":3,"maxLength":200,"pattern":"^(?![^/]+/[^;]*\\+xml(?:\\s*;|$))(?:(?:video|audio|image)/[a-z0-9!#$&^_.+-]+|application/(?:octet-stream|json)|text/plain)(?:\\s*;.*)?$","description":"The validated type the file is served with: video/*, audio/*, image/* except SVG or another +xml type, application/octet-stream, application/json, or text/plain. Other types, including HTML and XSL, are refused. Without it the file is served as application/octet-stream; the PUT Content-Type does not replace it."},"bytes":{"type":"integer","description":"No longer needed. Accepted and ignored."},"public_intent":{"type":"boolean","description":"No longer needed. Accepted and ignored."}},"required":[],"not":{"required":["files"]}},{"type":"object","properties":{"files":{"type":"array","minItems":1,"maxItems":256,"items":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":1024,"description":"Relative path in the bundle, with / between folders. No leading /, empty segment, . or .. segment, or backslash. One file must be index.html at the root."},"sha256":{"type":"string","pattern":"^[0-9a-f]{64}$","description":"SHA-256 of this file, in hex. A PUT whose bytes do not match is refused with digest_mismatch."},"bytes":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":100000000,"description":"Exact nonzero file length. The PUT Content-Length must match. Each file can be up to 100 MB."}},"required":["path","sha256","bytes"],"additionalProperties":false},"description":"Every regular file in the output folder from npx remotion bundle, including index.html. The sum of bytes can be at most 1 GB."}},"required":["files"],"additionalProperties":false}]}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"Success","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"oneOf":[{"type":"object","properties":{"upload_url":{"type":"string","format":"uri","description":"PUT the file bytes here with a Content-Length; the upload needs no key and returns 201. A place named by sha256 takes the same bytes again; any other place takes one upload. Refusals: 411 length_required (no Content-Length), 412 already_uploaded (the place already has its file), 400 digest_mismatch (the bytes are not the ones sha256 named), 404 not_found (no such place)."},"input_url":{"type":"string","format":"uri","description":"The public link of the uploaded file: the same address as upload_url. Use it in a job input. Every response carries Content-Security-Policy: sandbox; default-src 'none'. The file is kept for 24 hours. An upload can be up to 100 MB; pass a larger file by its own link."},"uploaded":{"type":"boolean","description":"Sent when the request named the file by sha256. true: the file is already stored and its link has at least 12 hours left, so there is nothing to upload."}},"required":["upload_url","input_url"]},{"type":"object","properties":{"serve_url":{"type":"string","format":"uri","description":"Public link to the bundle’s index.html on the isolated https://quiet-field-7f3c.buildngrowsv.workers.dev origin. Pass it as input.serve_url to remotion.render.v1 after every upload has returned 201. The bundle origin uses no API key, session or cookies, and the API origin does not serve bundle files."},"uploads":{"type":"array","minItems":1,"maxItems":256,"items":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"The relative bundle path named in the request."},"upload_url":{"type":"string","format":"uri","description":"PUT this file’s bytes here with a Content-Length equal to bytes. The upload needs no key and returns 201. The bytes must match its sha256. Refusals: 411 length_required (no Content-Length), 400 size_mismatch or digest_mismatch, 404 not_found (the bundle or path was not prepared)."},"content_type":{"type":"string","description":"The type the file is served with, inferred from its path. The PUT Content-Type does not replace it."}},"required":["path","upload_url","content_type"]},"description":"One upload for every requested file. PUT all of them, including files uploaded before; another PUT of the declared bytes is accepted and renews its 24 hours."}},"required":["serve_url","uploads"]}]}}}},"400":{"description":"invalid_bundle: files is empty or over the limit, index.html is missing, a file is empty, a path is unsafe or repeated, bytes or a SHA-256 is missing, or an unknown field was sent. bundle_too_large: the files total more than 1 GB. size_mismatch or digest_mismatch: uploaded bytes do not match the manifest. invalid_content_type: a single upload named a type outside the documented media allowlist.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Error"}}}},"503":{"description":"bundle_origin_unavailable: bundle hosting is not configured; no manifest or upload links were created.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Error"}}}},"default":{"description":"Request error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Error"}}}}}}},"/v1/jobs":{"post":{"operationId":"submitJob","tags":["Jobs"],"summary":"Submit a job","description":"Creates a job and returns it as queued. Poll GET /v1/jobs/{id} until the status is final. A job is charged once, when it succeeds: H3 at the price of its options, FFmpeg and Remotion work for the length of the output, and an image or a measurement at one flat price. Failed, cancelled and expired jobs cost nothing. An organization can have 8 jobs running and 50 queued.","requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Specification"}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"The same key and the same request were submitted before. The original job is returned and nothing new is created or charged, so a submit that got no answer can be sent again to learn the job ID. The whole request is compared: service_id, input, max_wait_seconds, client_reference, priority and webhook_endpoint_id. A key is remembered as long as its job is.","headers":{"Idempotency-Replayed":{"schema":{"type":"string","enum":["true"]}}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Job"}}}},"201":{"description":"Success","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Job"}}}},"400":{"description":"The request was refused. invalid_request carries an issues list naming each field. valid_idempotency_key_header_required: the Idempotency-Key header is missing, or is not 8 to 128 characters. unsupported_service_or_option: the service is not sold or an option is not offered.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Error"}}}},"402":{"description":"insufficient_balance: the prepaid balance does not cover this job, or an amount is due for finished work. Add funds and submit again.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Error"}}}},"409":{"description":"idempotency_conflict: this Idempotency-Key was already used with a different body. no_capacity: no renderer can take this service now, or its queue is full; submit again later.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Error"}}}},"429":{"description":"shared_beta_org_active_limit: the organization already has 8 jobs running; a further submit is refused, not queued. shared_beta_org_queue_limit: it already has 50 queued. Submit again when one finishes. A key may also submit 120 jobs a minute. rate_limited: a request limit was passed; wait for the Retry-After seconds.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Error"}}}},"default":{"description":"Request error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Error"}}}}},"parameters":[{"name":"Idempotency-Key","in":"header","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","minLength":8,"maxLength":128},"description":"A unique value for this submission. Repeating a submission with the same key and the same body returns the original job and does not create or charge a second one."}]},"get":{"operationId":"listJobs","tags":["Jobs"],"summary":"List your jobs","responses":{"200":{"description":"Success","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"jobs":{"type":"array","items":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Job"}},"next_cursor":{"type":["string","null"],"description":"Opaque cursor for the next page, or null when there are no more jobs."}},"required":["jobs","next_cursor"]}}}},"default":{"description":"Request error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Error"}}}}},"parameters":[{"name":"status","in":"query","schema":{"type":"string"},"description":"Return only jobs with this status: queued, active, cancelling, succeeded, failed, cancelled, expired. Another value is refused with 400 invalid_status."},{"name":"limit","in":"query","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":200,"default":50},"description":"Maximum number of jobs to return."},{"name":"cursor","in":"query","schema":{"type":"string"},"description":"Opaque next_cursor from the previous response. Omit for the first page."}],"description":"Newest first."}},"/v1/jobs/estimate":{"post":{"operationId":"estimateJob","tags":["Jobs"],"summary":"Check the price and capacity for a job","description":"Takes the same service_id and input as a job. It creates no job, reserves nothing and does not fetch or store media. For H3 the price is final for the given options. For FFmpeg, measurement and Remotion work it is an estimate, because the charge follows the length of the output. Remotion price_micros does not come from opening the bundle or reading the composition. It is based on frame_range when provided (the inclusive frame count divided by 30 fps), or a 20-second default when frame_range is absent. It is not the final charge: price_is_final is false, and the completed job is charged for its actual output.","requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/EstimateRequest"}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"Success","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Estimate"}}}},"400":{"description":"The request was refused. invalid_request carries an issues list naming each field.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Error"}}}},"default":{"description":"Request error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Error"}}}}}}},"/v1/jobs/{id}":{"parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","format":"uuid"}}],"get":{"operationId":"getJob","tags":["Jobs"],"summary":"Read job status and charges","responses":{"200":{"description":"Success","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Job"}}}},"default":{"description":"Request error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Error"}}}}}}},"/v1/jobs/{id}/output":{"parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","format":"uuid"}}],"get":{"operationId":"getJobOutput","tags":["Jobs"],"summary":"Get the public link of the finished file","description":"The link of the one file a succeeded job made. Fetch it with a plain GET; it needs no key and takes byte ranges.","responses":{"200":{"description":"Success","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"url":{"type":"string","format":"uri","description":"A plain public link. The file is kept for 3 days after the render finishes; after that the link answers 404."}},"required":["url"]}}}},"409":{"description":"output_not_ready: the job has not succeeded, so it has no file.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Error"}}}},"default":{"description":"Request error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Error"}}}}}}},"/v1/jobs/{id}/cancel":{"parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","format":"uuid"}}],"post":{"operationId":"cancelJob","tags":["Jobs"],"summary":"Cancel a job","description":"Send an empty JSON object. A queued job becomes cancelled at once. A job that is rendering becomes cancelling, then cancelled when its renderer stops; job.cancelled is sent then. A job already in a final state is returned as it is. A cancelled job is not charged.","requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{},"required":[]}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"Success","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Job"}}}},"default":{"description":"Request error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Error"}}}}}}},"/v1/webhook-endpoints":{"post":{"operationId":"createWebhookEndpoint","tags":["Webhooks"],"summary":"Register a webhook endpoint","description":"When a job reaches a final state PennyCompute sends a POST with a JSON body {id, type, data} to each active endpoint subscribed to that event. type is job.succeeded, job.failed (also sent when a queued job expires, with status expired) or job.cancelled. data carries job_id and status, and failure_code with a message when the job did not succeed. id is the delivery ID. Each request has X-PennyCompute-Event, X-PennyCompute-Delivery (the same ID, the same on every attempt) and X-PennyCompute-Attempt headers. The first attempt is sent as soon as the job has ended, or within 3 seconds for a job that ends with no word from a renderer; by then GET /v1/jobs/{id} already reads the final state, the charge and the output link. Answer with any 2xx within ten seconds; a redirect counts as a failure. After another answer the delivery is sent again after 5 seconds, 30 seconds, 2 minutes, 10 minutes, 1 hour, 6 hours and 12 hours, 8 attempts in all over about 19 hours; a Retry-After on your answer, up to a day, replaces the next wait. A delivery can arrive more than once, so act on a delivery ID once. Read the job with GET /v1/jobs/{id} for its charge and GET /v1/jobs/{id}/output for the file.","requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":80},"url":{"type":"string","format":"uri","description":"A public HTTPS URL."},"events":{"type":"array","minItems":1,"items":{"enum":["job.succeeded","job.failed","job.cancelled"]},"default":["job.succeeded"]}},"required":["name","url"],"additionalProperties":false}}}},"responses":{"201":{"description":"Success","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"endpoint":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/WebhookEndpoint"}},"required":["endpoint"]}}}},"400":{"description":"invalid_webhook_url: the URL is not HTTPS or does not lead to a public address. invalid_request: a field was refused.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Error"}}}},"409":{"description":"webhook_conflict: an active endpoint with this URL already exists. A URL that was removed can be registered again: the endpoint comes back active under the same id, with the new name and events.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Error"}}}},"default":{"description":"Request error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Error"}}}}}},"get":{"operationId":"listWebhookEndpoints","tags":["Webhooks"],"summary":"List webhook endpoints","description":"Newest first. A removed endpoint stays in the list with status disabled.","responses":{"200":{"description":"Success","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"endpoints":{"type":"array","items":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/WebhookEndpoint"}}},"required":["endpoints"]}}}},"default":{"description":"Request error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Error"}}}}}}},"/v1/webhook-endpoints/{id}":{"parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","format":"uuid"}}],"delete":{"operationId":"removeWebhookEndpoint","tags":["Webhooks"],"summary":"Remove a webhook endpoint","description":"Stops deliveries to it, including pending retries. The endpoint stays in the list with status disabled. Registering its URL again brings it back active under the same id.","responses":{"204":{"description":"Removed"},"404":{"description":"not_found: no such endpoint, or it was already removed.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Error"}}}},"default":{"description":"Request error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Error"}}}}}}},"/v1/billing/balance":{"get":{"operationId":"getBalance","tags":["Billing"],"summary":"Read the prepaid balance","responses":{"200":{"description":"Success","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"prepaid_micros":{"type":"string","pattern":"^[0-9]+$","description":"Funds added and not yet charged, in millionths of one US dollar. A new account starts at 5000000, $5."},"outstanding_micros":{"type":"string","pattern":"^[0-9]+$","description":"Charges for finished work that the balance did not cover. The next top-up pays them first, and a job submit answers 402 until they are paid."}},"required":["prepaid_micros","outstanding_micros"]}}}},"default":{"description":"Request error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Error"}}}}}}},"/v1/billing/top-up":{"post":{"operationId":"startTopUp","tags":["Dashboard"],"summary":"Start a card top-up","description":"Add funds in the dashboard: it opens the checkout page this call returns. A dashboard call: it needs a signed-in person whose role allows it, and a server API key gets 403.","requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"amount_usd":{"type":"number","minimum":1,"maximum":50000,"description":"Whole cents."}},"required":["amount_usd"]}}}},"responses":{"201":{"description":"Success","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"checkout_url":{"type":"string","format":"uri"},"stripe_session_id":{"type":"string"}},"required":["checkout_url"]}}}},"default":{"description":"Request error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Error"}}}}},"parameters":[{"name":"Idempotency-Key","in":"header","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","pattern":"^[a-zA-Z0-9_-]{8,100}$"}}]}},"/v1/usage":{"get":{"operationId":"listUsage","tags":["Billing"],"summary":"List charges and usage entries","description":"One entry per charge, newest first. A parameter the call does not know is refused with 400 invalid_request.","responses":{"200":{"description":"Success","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"usage":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"job_id":{"type":["string","null"]},"instance_id":{"type":"string","description":"Set on the charge of a container instance, with its label and running seconds."},"label":{"type":["string","null"]},"running_seconds":{"type":"integer"},"kind":{"type":"string","enum":["job_execution","instance"],"description":"job_execution: the charge of one succeeded job."},"amount_micros":{"type":"string","pattern":"^[0-9]+$","description":"Millionths of one US dollar"},"created_at":{"type":"string"}},"required":[]}},"next_cursor":{"type":["string","null"],"description":"Cursor for the next page, or null when there are no more entries."}},"required":["usage"]}}}},"default":{"description":"Request error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Error"}}}}},"parameters":[{"name":"since","in":"query","schema":{"type":"string","format":"date-time"},"description":"Entries created at or after this time. A date-time with an offset, such as 2026-11-01T00:00:00Z."},{"name":"until","in":"query","schema":{"type":"string","format":"date-time"},"description":"Entries created before this time. It has to be later than since, or the answer is 400 invalid_period."},{"name":"limit","in":"query","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":200,"default":50}},{"name":"cursor","in":"query","schema":{"type":"string"},"description":"next_cursor from the previous page."}]}},"/v1/invoices":{"get":{"operationId":"listInvoices","tags":["Billing"],"summary":"List invoices","description":"One statement for each calendar month (UTC) with charges, newest first. A statement id is st_ and the month, such as st_2026-11. The current month is a draft; a past month is issued.","responses":{"200":{"description":"Success","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"invoices":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"currency":{"type":"string"},"status":{"type":"string"},"period_start":{"type":"string"},"period_end":{"type":"string"},"total_micros":{"type":"string","pattern":"^[0-9]+$","description":"Millionths of one US dollar"},"created_at":{"type":"string"}},"required":[]}}},"required":["invoices"]}}}},"default":{"description":"Request error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Error"}}}}},"parameters":[{"name":"limit","in":"query","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":200,"default":50}}]}},"/v1/auth/me":{"get":{"operationId":"getIdentity","tags":["Account"],"summary":"Read who is calling","description":"A quick check that a key works: it answers for any key that is not revoked.","responses":{"200":{"description":"Success","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"auth_type":{"type":"string","enum":["api_key","member_session"],"description":"api_key for a server API key; member_session for a person signed in to the dashboard."},"org_id":{"type":"string","format":"uuid"},"api_key_id":{"type":"string","format":"uuid","description":"Set for a key."},"scopes":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"description":"Set for a key."},"member":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string","format":"uuid"},"display_name":{"type":"string"},"email":{"type":"string"},"role":{"type":"string","enum":["owner","admin","developer","billing"],"description":"owner: everything, including acting on other owners. admin: everything except acting on owners. developer: jobs, uploads, instances, images, webhooks and server API keys. billing: adds funds and reads jobs, usage and statements."}},"required":[],"description":"Set for a signed-in person."},"organization":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string","format":"uuid"},"name":{"type":"string"}},"required":[]}},"required":["auth_type","org_id","organization"]}}}},"default":{"description":"Request error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Error"}}}}}}},"/v1/org/api-keys":{"get":{"operationId":"listApiKeys","tags":["Dashboard"],"summary":"List server API keys","description":"Every key of the organization, oldest first, revoked ones included. A dashboard call: it needs a signed-in person whose role allows it, and a server API key gets 403.","responses":{"200":{"description":"Success","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"api_keys":{"type":"array","items":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKey"}}},"required":["api_keys"]}}}},"default":{"description":"Request error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Error"}}}}}},"post":{"operationId":"createApiKey","tags":["Dashboard"],"summary":"Create a server API key","description":"Create keys under Server API keys in the dashboard. A dashboard call: it needs a signed-in person whose role allows it, and a server API key gets 403.","requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":120},"scopes":{"type":"array","minItems":1,"items":{"type":"string","enum":["jobs:read","jobs:write"]}}},"required":["name","scopes"]}}}},"responses":{"201":{"description":"Success","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"api_key":{"type":"string","description":"The key. Shown once."},"record":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKey"}},"required":["api_key","record"]}}}},"default":{"description":"Request error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Error"}}}}}}},"/v1/org/api-keys/{id}/revoke":{"parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","format":"uuid"}}],"post":{"operationId":"revokeApiKey","tags":["Dashboard"],"summary":"Revoke a server API key","description":"A revoked key no longer works. A dashboard call: it needs a signed-in person whose role allows it, and a server API key gets 403.","requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{},"required":[]}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"Success","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"ok":{"type":"boolean"},"record":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ApiKey"}},"required":[]}}}},"default":{"description":"Request error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Error"}}}}}}},"/v1/org/members":{"get":{"operationId":"listMembers","tags":["Dashboard"],"summary":"List the people in the organization","description":"Everyone in the organization, oldest first, and the invitations not yet used or expired. Anyone signed in to the organization can read it. A dashboard call: it needs a signed-in person whose role allows it, and a server API key gets 403.","responses":{"200":{"description":"Success","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"members":{"type":"array","items":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Member"}},"invitations":{"type":"array","items":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Invitation"}}},"required":["members","invitations"]}}}},"default":{"description":"Request error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Error"}}}}}}},"/v1/org/members/{id}":{"parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","format":"uuid"}}],"post":{"operationId":"changeMemberRole","tags":["Dashboard"],"summary":"Change a role","description":"Owners and admins change roles; only an owner makes or changes an owner. The new role applies to the person's next call. 409 last_owner: an organization keeps at least one owner. A dashboard call: it needs a signed-in person whose role allows it, and a server API key gets 403.","requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"role":{"type":"string","enum":["owner","admin","developer","billing"],"description":"owner: everything, including acting on other owners. admin: everything except acting on owners. developer: jobs, uploads, instances, images, webhooks and server API keys. billing: adds funds and reads jobs, usage and statements."}},"required":["role"]}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"Success","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"member":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Member"}},"required":["member"]}}}},"default":{"description":"Request error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Error"}}}}}},"delete":{"operationId":"removeMember","tags":["Dashboard"],"summary":"Remove a person","description":"Their sessions end at once. 409 last_owner: an organization keeps at least one owner. A dashboard call: it needs a signed-in person whose role allows it, and a server API key gets 403.","responses":{"204":{"description":"Removed"},"default":{"description":"Request error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Error"}}}}}}},"/v1/org/invitations":{"post":{"operationId":"inviteMember","tags":["Dashboard"],"summary":"Invite a person","description":"Emails a link to join the organization with this role, good for seven days. Inviting the same address again replaces the invitation. 409 account_exists: the address already has a PennyCompute account. A dashboard call: it needs a signed-in person whose role allows it, and a server API key gets 403.","requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"email":{"type":"string"},"role":{"type":"string","enum":["owner","admin","developer","billing"],"description":"owner: everything, including acting on other owners. admin: everything except acting on owners. developer: jobs, uploads, instances, images, webhooks and server API keys. billing: adds funds and reads jobs, usage and statements."}},"required":["email","role"]}}}},"responses":{"201":{"description":"Success","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"invitation":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Invitation"}},"required":["invitation"]}}}},"default":{"description":"Request error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Error"}}}}}}},"/v1/org/invitations/{id}":{"parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","format":"uuid"}}],"delete":{"operationId":"cancelInvitation","tags":["Dashboard"],"summary":"Cancel an invitation","description":"Its link stops working. A dashboard call: it needs a signed-in person whose role allows it, and a server API key gets 403.","responses":{"204":{"description":"Cancelled"},"default":{"description":"Request error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Error"}}}}}}},"/healthz":{"get":{"operationId":"getHealth","tags":["Status"],"summary":"Read whether the API is up","security":[],"description":"Needs no key. 200 when the API, the service catalog and payments are working; 503 with the same body when the catalog is unavailable or top-ups are settling late.","responses":{"200":{"description":"Working","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"api":{"enum":["available"]},"catalog":{"enum":["available","unavailable"],"description":"Whether jobs can be submitted."},"payments":{"enum":["available","delayed","unknown"],"description":"Whether a top-up reaches the balance promptly."},"instances":{"enum":["available","unavailable"],"description":"Whether a container instance could be started now."},"settlement":{"enum":["available","delayed","unknown"],"description":"Whether charges for finished work reach the balance within a few minutes."}},"required":["api","catalog","payments"]}}}},"503":{"description":"Not fully working","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"api":{"enum":["available"]},"catalog":{"enum":["available","unavailable"],"description":"Whether jobs can be submitted."},"payments":{"enum":["available","delayed","unknown"],"description":"Whether a top-up reaches the balance promptly."},"instances":{"enum":["available","unavailable"],"description":"Whether a container instance could be started now."},"settlement":{"enum":["available","delayed","unknown"],"description":"Whether charges for finished work reach the balance within a few minutes."}},"required":["api","catalog","payments"]}}}}}}},"/v1/images":{"post":{"operationId":"registerImage","tags":["Images"],"summary":"Register an image","description":"Push the image to a registry of your own with ordinary tooling, then register its reference here. PennyCompute copies it once and serves it to the machines; your registry is not read again. Registering a digest that is already held returns it.","requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ImageSource"}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"Already registered","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Image"}}}},"202":{"description":"Success","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Image"}}}},"default":{"description":"Request error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string"}},"required":["error"]}}}}}},"get":{"operationId":"listImages","tags":["Images"],"summary":"List your images","description":"Every registered image with its state.","responses":{"200":{"description":"Success","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"images":{"type":"array","items":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Image"}}},"required":["images"]}}}},"default":{"description":"Request error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string"}},"required":["error"]}}}}}}},"/v1/images/{digest}":{"parameters":[{"name":"digest","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","pattern":"^sha256:[0-9a-f]{64}$","description":"The image digest, as printed by the push to your registry."}}],"get":{"operationId":"getImage","tags":["Images"],"summary":"Read whether the machines hold an image","description":"An instance can be started once the state is held.","responses":{"200":{"description":"Success","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Image"}}}},"default":{"description":"Request error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string"}},"required":["error"]}}}}}}},"/v1/images/{digest}/remove":{"parameters":[{"name":"digest","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","pattern":"^sha256:[0-9a-f]{64}$","description":"The image digest, as printed by the push to your registry."}}],"post":{"operationId":"removeImage","tags":["Images"],"summary":"Remove an image","description":"Deletes the stored copy. Running instances keep running.","requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{},"required":[]}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"Success","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"removed":{"const":true},"digest":{"type":"string","pattern":"^sha256:[0-9a-f]{64}$","description":"The image digest, as printed by the push to your registry."}},"required":["removed"]}}}},"default":{"description":"Request error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string"}},"required":["error"]}}}}}}},"/v1/instances":{"post":{"operationId":"startInstance","tags":["Instances"],"summary":"Start an instance by name","description":"Answers at once: started, or refused with a reason. There is no queue. 201 is a new instance; 200 is the instance already starting or running under this name, returned whatever the body asks for. Any other answer means no instance is left running by this call.","requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/InstanceStart"}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"The instance already running under this name","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Instance"}}}},"201":{"description":"Success","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Instance"}}}},"409":{"description":"Refused. No instance was started and nothing is charged. no_capacity: no machine is free for this size now. image_not_held: no machine holds the image yet. account: the balance is empty or an amount is due. instance_limit: your running instances are at your limit.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string","enum":["no_capacity","image_not_held","account","instance_limit"]}},"required":["error"]}}}},"503":{"description":"Instances cannot be started now. No instance was started.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string","enum":["instances_unavailable"]}},"required":["error"]}}}},"default":{"description":"Request error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string"}},"required":["error"]}}}}}},"get":{"operationId":"listInstances","tags":["Instances"],"summary":"List instances","description":"Newest first. With from and to, the instances that ran in that time: usage per instance.","parameters":[{"name":"state","in":"query","schema":{"type":"string","enum":["starting","running","stopped","crashed","lost"]}},{"name":"label","in":"query","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"name":"name","in":"query","schema":{"type":"string"},"description":"The current or most recent instance with this name."},{"name":"from","in":"query","schema":{"type":"string","format":"date-time"},"description":"Instances that ran at or after this time."},{"name":"to","in":"query","schema":{"type":"string","format":"date-time"},"description":"Instances that ran before this time."},{"name":"limit","in":"query","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":200,"default":50}},{"name":"cursor","in":"query","schema":{"type":"string"},"description":"next_cursor from the previous page."}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Success","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"instances":{"type":"array","items":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Instance"}},"next_cursor":{"type":["string","null"]}},"required":["instances","next_cursor"]}}}},"default":{"description":"Request error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string"}},"required":["error"]}}}}}}},"/v1/instances/usage":{"get":{"operationId":"getInstanceUsage","tags":["Instances"],"summary":"Read usage and charges by label","description":"Running seconds and charges of the instances that ended in a time range, totalled per label.","parameters":[{"name":"from","in":"query","schema":{"type":"string","format":"date-time"}},{"name":"to","in":"query","schema":{"type":"string","format":"date-time"}},{"name":"label","in":"query","schema":{"type":"string"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Success","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"from":{"type":"string","format":"date-time"},"to":{"type":"string","format":"date-time"},"usage":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"label":{"type":["string","null"]},"instances":{"type":"integer"},"running_seconds":{"type":"integer"},"charge_micros":{"type":"string","pattern":"^[0-9]+$","description":"Millionths of one US dollar"}},"required":["label","charge_micros"]}},"total_charge_micros":{"type":"string","pattern":"^[0-9]+$","description":"Millionths of one US dollar"}},"required":["usage","total_charge_micros"]}}}},"default":{"description":"Request error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string"}},"required":["error"]}}}}}}},"/v1/instances/destroy":{"post":{"operationId":"destroyInstanceNamed","tags":["Instances"],"summary":"Destroy the instance with a name","description":"For a caller that knows only the name, such as one that abandoned a start. Takes effect at once.","requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string"}},"required":["name"]}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"Success","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"destroyed":{"type":"boolean"},"instance":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Instance"}},"required":["destroyed"]}}}},"default":{"description":"Request error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string"}},"required":["error"]}}}}}}},"/v1/instances/{id}":{"parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string"}}],"get":{"operationId":"getInstance","tags":["Instances"],"summary":"Read state, running seconds and the charge so far","description":"The token is not returned here.","responses":{"200":{"description":"Success","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Instance"}}}},"default":{"description":"Request error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string"}},"required":["error"]}}}}}}},"/v1/instances/{id}/destroy":{"parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string"}}],"post":{"operationId":"destroyInstance","tags":["Instances"],"summary":"Destroy an instance","description":"Takes effect at once: the address stops answering and billing stops. Repeating it is harmless.","requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{},"required":[]}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"Success","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/Instance"}}}},"default":{"description":"Request error","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"string"}},"required":["error"]}}}}}}}},"webhooks":{"jobEvent":{"post":{"operationId":"receiveJobEvent","tags":["Webhooks"],"summary":"A job reached a final state","description":"When a job reaches a final state PennyCompute sends a POST with a JSON body {id, type, data} to each active endpoint subscribed to that event. type is job.succeeded, job.failed (also sent when a queued job expires, with status expired) or job.cancelled. data carries job_id and status, and failure_code with a message when the job did not succeed. id is the delivery ID. Each request has X-PennyCompute-Event, X-PennyCompute-Delivery (the same ID, the same on every attempt) and X-PennyCompute-Attempt headers. The first attempt is sent as soon as the job has ended, or within 3 seconds for a job that ends with no word from a renderer; by then GET /v1/jobs/{id} already reads the final state, the charge and the output link. Answer with any 2xx within ten seconds; a redirect counts as a failure. After another answer the delivery is sent again after 5 seconds, 30 seconds, 2 minutes, 10 minutes, 1 hour, 6 hours and 12 hours, 8 attempts in all over about 19 hours; a Retry-After on your answer, up to a day, replaces the next wait. A delivery can arrive more than once, so act on a delivery ID once. Read the job with GET /v1/jobs/{id} for its charge and GET /v1/jobs/{id}/output for the file.","security":[],"parameters":[{"name":"X-PennyCompute-Event","in":"header","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string"},"description":"The event type."},{"name":"X-PennyCompute-Delivery","in":"header","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string"},"description":"The delivery ID."},{"name":"X-PennyCompute-Attempt","in":"header","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string"},"description":"Which attempt this is, from 1."}],"requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/WebhookEvent"}}}},"responses":{"2XX":{"description":"Received. Any other answer is sent again."}}}}}}